{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","title":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.md","line":53,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","label":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","line":129,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Bishop--Gromov relative volume comparison]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0294,petersen:page-0295}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.1.4}\n  Let $(M,g)$ be complete with $\\Ric\\ge(n-1)k$. The volume ratio\n  \\[\n    r\\mapsto\\frac{\\vol B(p,r)}{v(n,k,r)}\n  \\]\n  is a nonincreasing function of $r$, with limit $1$ as $r\\to0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature}, \\(N'(R)/D'(R)\\) is the spherical average of the nonincreasing ratios \\(\\lambda/\\lambda_k\\), where \\(N(R)=\\vol B(p,R)\\) and \\(D(R)=v(n,k,R)\\). Differentiating \\(N/D\\) proves monotonicity, and the common polar-density asymptotic gives the limit \\(1\\) at \\(0\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Bishop--Gromov relative volume comparison] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368372d72656c61746976652d766f6c756d652d636f6d70617269736f6e\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0294, petersen:page-0295</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch7:7.1.4</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> be complete with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$\">$\\Ric \\ge (n-1)k$</span>. The volume ratio <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  r\\mapsto \\frac{\\vol B(p,r)}{v(n,k,r)}  \\]\">\\[  r\\mapsto \\frac{\\vol B(p,r)}{v(n,k,r)}  \\]</span> is a nonincreasing function of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r$\">$r$</span>, with limit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> as <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r\\to 0$\">$r\\to 0$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison\">↗ lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison</a> \\sketch By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh07_RicciCurvatureComparison%23lem%3Apet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368372d72696363692d636f6d70617269736f6e2d6d65616e2d637572766174757265\">subsection 1.2</a>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N&#x27;(R)/D&#x27;(R)$\">$N&#x27;(R)/D&#x27;(R)$</span> is the spherical average of the nonincreasing ratios <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda /\\lambda _k$\">$\\lambda /\\lambda _k$</span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N(R)=\\vol B(p,R)$\">$N(R)=\\vol B(p,R)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$D(R)=v(n,k,R)$\">$D(R)=v(n,k,R)$</span>. Differentiating <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$N/D$\">$N/D$</span> proves monotonicity, and the common polar-density asymptotic gives the limit <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0$\">$0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-absolute-volume-comparison","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-hessian-touching-comparison","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature","title":"lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature","label":"lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","title":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","label":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","title":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","label":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","title":"cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare","label":"cor:pet-ch7-weak-poincare"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem","label":"thm:pet-ch7-maximal-function-theorem"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#thm:pet-ch7-weak-poincare-sobolev-estimate","title":"thm:pet-ch7-weak-poincare-sobolev-estimate","label":"thm:pet-ch7-weak-poincare-sobolev-estimate"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-10","title":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-10","label":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-10"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#rem:pet-ch7-ex-18","title":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-18","label":"rem:pet-ch7-ex-18"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","title":"lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Bishop--Gromov relative volume comparison]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0294,petersen:page-0295}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature}\n  \\dcref{ch7:7.1.4}\n  Let $(M,g)$ be complete with $\\Ric\\ge(n-1)k$. The volume ratio\n  \\[\n    r\\mapsto\\frac{\\vol B(p,r)}{v(n,k,r)}\n  \\]\n  is a nonincreasing function of $r$, with limit $1$ as $r\\to0$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch7-relative-volume-comparison}\n  \\sketch\n  By \\cref{lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature}, \\(N'(R)/D'(R)\\) is the spherical average of the nonincreasing ratios \\(\\lambda/\\lambda_k\\), where \\(N(R)=\\vol B(p,R)\\) and \\(D(R)=v(n,k,R)\\). Differentiating \\(N/D\\) proves monotonicity, and the common polar-density asymptotic gives the limit \\(1\\) at \\(0\\).\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch07_RicciCurvatureComparison#lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature","title":"lem:pet-ch7-ricci-comparison-mean-curvature","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}